<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Complutensian Polyglot Bible</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1514">1514</a>–<a href="/years/1517">1517</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Complutensian Polyglot Bible was the first printed polyglot edition of the whole Bible, prepared at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-alcala">University of Alcalá</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/complutum">Complutum</a>, under the patronage of Cardinal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-jimenez-de-cisneros">Francisco Jiménez de Cisneros</a>. Printed in six volumes between 1514 and 1517 and issued in the early 1520s, it set the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a>, Greek and Latin texts side by side.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/complutensian-polyglot-bible.jpg" alt="Complutensian Polyglot Bible" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francisco Jiménez de Cisneros (Uploaded by MaiDireLollo) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cisneros%27_original_complutensian_polyglot_Bible_-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
